{.i go'i .i ku'i zo.a'o na lacri zo.ia .i.uenai ma'a noroi cilre roda rode
.iku'i na.a'o go'i}
Agreed, but hope is not dependent on belief. I expect we will never learn
everything, but I hope we do.


> ra'u nai, is there an afterthought construct that will let me put two full
> bridi in one abstraction? {.i bo} doesn't seem to do it, and {ju'e} and
> {gi'e} both do bridi tails.
>

I don't think so. You can't use anything with .i, because the .i kills
everything and starts a new main level bridi. There's GA...gi..., but
that's forethought, and I don't think there's an afterthought equivalent. I
could be wrong, of course, but I'm not aware of anything.


